{
  "id": "f03",
  "rule": "block types (/wp/v2/block-types, Part G b12, b14): the test block type qp-it/notice (a title, the category text, one declared attribute and a renderer) with the attributes its default supports add, is_dynamic and the renderer link, for a contributor, refused for a subscriber (403) and anonymous (401); an unknown type refused by the permission check (404 without Allow); a namespace's collection; the query's namespace beating the URL's; names compared exactly while routes match ignoring case; the context checked against its enum; OPTIONS of a type and of a namespace's collection; the attributes block supports add and where style goes, on the probe types of the qp_parity_block_types switch (qp-probe/*: one support or two each) and acme/supports; WordPress's core types, which QuarkPress does not register (D50)",
  "setup": [
    {
      "option": "qp_parity_notice_block",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "option": "qp_parity_block_types",
      "value": "1"
    }
  ],
